From bdb4872a9811e748b845af9320f0017d97c90893 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Marius Gehrmann <marius@gehrmann.solutions>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 21:12:49 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 08/12] soc: apple: rtkit: Honour apple,sync-syslog-ack

Port the RTKit part of AsahiLinux/linux#607, which the T8122 dcpext
firmware needs (its J613 device tree node carries apple,sync-syslog-ack):
- acknowledge syslog log messages and ioreport notifications (types 0x8
  and 0xc) right away, ahead of the other receive work;
- start the kdebug endpoint and hand out its two buffers;
- poll the mailbox while waiting for the boot handshake and power-state
  acknowledgments;
- leave OSLOG_LOG notifications unacknowledged, as #607 does. The
  firmware then sends one and keeps its log to itself.

AsahiLinux/linux#607 sends those acknowledgments from the receive path
with an atomic mailbox send, which can spin for up to the 500 ms TX
timeout in hard IRQ context under the mailbox locks if the FIFO is full.
Here the receive path only puts them on a small ring, and a work item on
the high priority system workqueue sends them from process context. If
the ring is full, the message takes the ordinary path, which
acknowledges it too. A failed acknowledgment is logged. The kdebug
buffers and the other shared buffers now use one allocation helper.

Aurora's RTKit already returns start_ep errors, which #607 also adds.
Unlike #607, all of this is gated on the property, so every other
co-processor (the internal DCP's adopted session, SMC, ANS, ...) behaves
exactly as before. #607's mailbox change (I2A FIFO enable) is for
apple,t6030-asc-mailbox and is not needed on T8122.

Link: https://github.com/AsahiLinux/linux/pull/607
